<description>&lt;p&gt;Government forces and opposition fighters continue to clash, most recently in Akobo, while governors in Jonglei and Aweil East call for peace ahead of the first elections scheduled for next month. Ugandan truck drivers were ambushed and killed, and their bodies were later released by South Sudanese authorities. The Mayom County commissioner and his family were assassinated, and a soldier and a civilian were killed in an attack in Kapoeta North. Communal fighting in Tonj East left eleven dead before calm returned, and churches reported worship disruptions due to violence. The UCDP recorded two battle-related deaths in 2024.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMixwFBVV95cUxQX2luRkZSZ3VaTUZMd1hDMUJqaGNnQThhNlgzX0FQZWFMbDhjN2R2ZjJIdUZzb0UwMlNkRjhXRWpwUjZOMkFaZG5hczhyZ2ZMcDBtbHBhMFpwYVpmdG1GWEJnSFVIWEUtdEphMzdrRmJGMFE0bmljOFl4TlZJTEZyOVNRSXVWUno0SEROM09FSXM4WndZemx1XzFldVJIanNZQjNzYnJiOFZhYkhjeEFpam1yTkFCYTlxQkU1d2FScVR4UTUtWU04?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Washington Post&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMikAFBVV95cUxPMkdlVHNvZldMbFRyX1hhbG9Hc2VsbUVZOTJGZDFDYndEc05ZN3NGaGFRaDZuQWNzeVJaS2JMNk9RNzlVOUx3UHVWeWFfYnZjMWlJa0xDNV9UMzRoTnpSaFpzWF80UDNyS2EwRmZhX05KWElDV3VpODdfcm03SzFaR3hZbTRkdVpqWG1aMnpYSTE?oc=5&quot;&gt;ReliefWeb&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiX0FVX3lxTE9iNjRyY1lQSmpERVBvc2lqb21UeXF1NDhsTnE1c0ZkOWtnWG1uaU9QbHJjMjFmMXB1dFJJTnI0OGluSVhDWjRqQ0pfTENEbzUweWw0VUlJLXRjR1J6MGlR0gFkQVVfeXFMTkoxTVpvR3hxV1pSbGZfR3dTV0x2eVJGNW96N2ZhUFlVb0lHdjlVZXB0SVRJa19ESk5RQllhSWJlMWFacE52QU9jSEZwdzlldkJDcTZ2cnZJTDZtVDJCQmRtTUhmbg?oc=5&quot;&gt;Global Issues.org&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiiAFBVV95cUxNMERadHF1NGsyWVptbmlzc09kUHhkdGh0ZnkyeE9TNF9lNUtVQ1p3NWtQTEJob1I3eWRNU1c0Z0RuUk5MR3pxeXlPenlDRXM4U1diWlk5cGE